@ [governing_goal] continue dependency-safe local Cantor work throughout the active five-hour shift without live-provider hidden-state persistence or external-effect operations

& [PreservedUserDirection]
  + "start another 5-hour turn"
  + a frame that exceeds available attention should be hashed for reentry so the job can continue in another bounded inference pass
  + executable attention procedures should recognize inputs outputs conditions and transforms while keeping the full hardened pattern behind a compact handle

& [InheritedIntention]
  + Cantor is the inference co-processor that loads an attention frame with the language needed to observe the current subject while exact state and proof remain under host custody
  + a current frame should settle before the next frame begins and a change of phase must be explicit rather than silently drifting inside one inference pass
  + speed and accuracy should come from organized concise expression whose meaning can be re-expanded and inspected

& [SelectedImplementationClaim]
  + activate a provider-free experimental AttentionReentryFrame compiled from a fully replay-valid nonempty iterative prefix
  + bind phase model session opening sequence iteration count retained-prefix digest current head sequence and handle digest latest call identity successor kind exact-custody flag privacy denial and nonclaims
  + calculate retained-prefix digest over deterministic compact JSON containing model prompt policy opening handle and the full admitted IterationRecord prefix
  + construct compact continuation and terminal-reflection requests from the original prompt compiled frame and only the latest exact assistant tool-call plus matching tool projection pair
  + preserve model tool schema host quota tool choice response schema temperature token bound and terminal-versus-advance phase from the full request
  + validate compact request by recomputing the frame full request expected compact request and structural surface correspondence from exact retained inputs
  + measure full versus compact requests over a quota-one multi-frame deterministic fixture to test whether compact request size remains bounded as full replay grows

& [SJSJustification]
  + Slice6A proves later stateless requests grow as earlier public call and projection pairs are replayed
  + the host already retains and replay-validates the full causal transcript so the model-facing request need not be the authoritative archive
  + a digest commitment makes omitted prior records addressable and tamper-evident without pretending the digest restores their semantic content inside the model
  + retaining the original prompt latest call pair and exact current projection gives the next pass its objective protocol continuity and current public state
  + structural request equivalence can be proven locally while semantic output equivalence remains an empirical live-model question outside this slice

& [Acceptance]
  + frame generation refuses empty invalid terminal-as-advance forked or mutated prefixes
  + changing prompt policy opening prefix call projection head phase digest or nonclaim makes frame validation fail
  + compact advance preserves the full request model tool function quota tool choice parallel flag thinking flag temperature and output bound
  + compact terminal reflection preserves the full request model disabled tools response schema terminal projection and output bound
  + latest assistant call and matching tool projection are byte-equal to the tail pair in the full request
  + quota-one fixture produces multiple reentry frames one terminal frame deterministic measurements and a checked-in artifact
  + measurement validates ordered iteration counts phases arithmetic reductions maximum compact size and full-prefix growth

& [Rollback]
  + P0 through Slice6A behavior remains unchanged and full transcript requests remain the authoritative default
  + removing the isolated experimental reentry-frame module exports artifact and tests removes Slice6B without migration

& [Boundary]
  + no replacement of full provider protocol no semantic-equivalence output-quality or provider-compatibility claim
  + no live provider model process HTTP socket tokenizer timing memory persistence concurrency remote EVO-X2 OneDrive hidden state KV cache live-token effect FPGA or Minecraft activation
